                'on submitting research proposal for ethics review Contact Policies Partnerships Programmes '
                'Publications Funding Opportunities Funding Opportunities External Grants Contact Search term Search '
                'Kisii University: Web People Search Web Other ways to search: Map Profiles Recent Posts Kisii '
                'University to Participate at the UNESCO Expert Meeting on 25-26 October 2023 Oct 18 2023 . Erick '
                'Oyaro Assessment of Indigenous knowledge and utilization of medicinal plants in management of '
                'COVID-19 in western Kenya and Harmful algal blooms in Lake Victoria Posted on Jan 22,2025 by Lead '
                'Researcher: Dr. Bethwell Owuor, PhD This research in Biotechnology focuses on utilizing indigenous '
                'African plant species for medicinal purposes, specifically in combating diseases like COVID-19 and '
                'monitoring harmful algal blooms in Lake Victoria. The project combines computational tools, machine '
                'learning, and next-generation sequencing technologies to explore traditional pharmacopoeia and '
                'analyze aquatic environmental DNA. This research, funded by major international organizations, is '
                'contributing to global health initiatives and advancing the understanding of biodiversity and its '
                'potential for sustainable health solutions. Important Links Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube QUICK '
