                'External Grants Contact Search term Search Kisii University: Web People Search Web Other ways to '
                'search: Map Profiles Recent Posts Kisii University to Participate at the UNESCO Expert Meeting on '
                '25-26 October 2023 Oct 18 2023 . Erick Oyaro Gender Equity in Climate Change Participation to Ensure '
                'Agroecological-Based Vegetable Production in Eastern Africa Posted on Jan 22,2025 by Lead Researcher: '
                'Dr. Jacquelyn Walubwa, PhD This project aims to address gender disparities in climate change '
                'adaptation, focusing on agro-ecological vegetable production. It emphasizes the inclusion of women '
                'and marginalized groups in climate change discussions and decision-making processes to improve '
                'resilience in Eastern Africa. By integrating gender-sensitive approaches, the project seeks to '
                'promote sustainable agricultural practices, ensuring food security and livelihood sustainability in '
