                'External Grants Contact Search term Search Kisii University: Web People Search Web Other ways to '
                'search: Map Profiles Recent Posts Kisii University to Participate at the UNESCO Expert Meeting on '
                '25-26 October 2023 Oct 18 2023 . Erick Oyaro Socio-Economic Vulnerabilities among Urban Migrants in '
                'the Lake Victoria Basin and Great Lakes Region Posted on Jan 22,2025 by Kenya lead researcher: Dr. '
                'Peter Gutwa Oino , PhD The Climate Adaptation and Resilience Strategies (CLARS) project, funded at '
                '$3.14 million from 2024 to 2027, seeks to reduce socio-economic vulnerabilities and enhance '
                'resilience to climate change for migrants and host communities in five cities: Kampala, Mwanza, '
                'Eldoret, Detroit, and Hamilton. Dr. Peter Gutwa leads the Kenyan segment of this interdisciplinary '
                'research, focusing on gender-sensitive climate adaptation strategies for climate migrants, especially '
                'women and girls in Kenya. The project combines participatory action research and climate knowledge '
                'exchange to address vulnerabilities and build strategies for more resilient urban migration responses '
                'in East Africa. Important Links Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube QUICK LINKS Funding Opportunities '
