                'Joseph Mogoi . Read Bio Joseph Mogoi Bio × Chemistry Technologists Close Dr. Hezron F. O. Ogutu COD '
                'Chemistry Read Bio Dr. Hezron F. O. Ogutu Bio × Dr. Hezron F. O. Ogutu • PhD in Chemistry. • SPAS, '
                'Department of Chemistry 3. Biography: • Dr. Hezron Ogutu is a seasoned Chemist, Department Faculty '
                'Lecturer, and currently serves as Chairman Department of chemistry, School of Pure and applied '
                'Science at Kisii University in Kenya, where he imparts his knowledge and passion for the field to '
                'aspiring chemists. Simultaneously, he serves as a board member at the centre of science technology '
                'and innovation, showcasing his commitment to applying scientific expertise in real-world contexts. '
                'With a robust educational background, having done his postdoctoral fellowship under mentorship of '
                'Prof Lueta De Kock at UNISA-INanoWS in South Africa, he also holds a PhD in hydrometallurgy chemistry '
                'from Stellenbosch University, an MSc in structural chemistry, from the University of Johannesburg, '
                "and a BSc in Industrial chemistry from the University of Nairobi. Dr. Ogutu's research interests are "
                'expansive and reflect his dedication to addressing sustainability and environmental challenges. His '
                'work spans green chemistry, mining chemistry, hydrometallurgy (with a focus on the synthesis of '
                'extractants), acid mine drainage, membrane synthesis, water remediation technology, and nanoparticles '
                'research. His proficiency in structural chemistry, utilizing techniques such as SXRD (Single Crystal '
                'X-ray Diffraction) and PXRD (Powder X-ray Diffraction), underscores his commitment to advancing the '
                'understanding of chemical structures. With his combination of academic and consultancy roles, Dr. '
                'Hezron Ogutu strives to make significant contributions to the realms of chemistry and environmental '
                'science. Sustainable eco-industrial growth can be achieved through innovative material structures. 4. '
                'Academic Qualifications: Type your Academic Qualifications here: • PhD: Stellenbosch University, '
                'South Africa • MSc: University of Johannesburg, South ||Africa • BSc. Industrial chemistry, '
                'University of Nairobi-Kenya 5. Research Interests: a) Hydrometallurgy research: Overview Lanthanides '
                'play a critical role in modern technologies necessitates the development of economical and scalable '
                'hydrometallurgical processes for their extraction from aqueous solutions. These rare earth elements '
                'exhibit complex and exceptional coordination chemistry, readily forming complexes with tailored '
                'ligands. This complexation behavior presents a powerful avenue for selective and efficient lanthanide '
                'separation, a crucial step for their industrial utilization e Title: • Synthesis of analogues Oxime '
                'Schiff base ligands for the hydrometallurgical extraction of Lanthanides and actinides collaboration '
                'with SU and UJ b) water remediation technology: overview: The presence of pollutants and their '
                'residues in water bodies has become a major environmental issue, requiring the development of '
                'efficient methods to address it. Project 1: photodegradation of emerging pollutants Tittle: • '
                'Photocatalytic degradation of selected pharmaceuticals in waste waters using iron/ graphite carbon '
                'nitride Collaboration with UNISA-InanoWS. Project 2: Green synthesis Tittle: • Green synthesis of '
                'iron nanoparticles for the remediation of phosphates and nitrates from waste water of river '
                'Naykomisare: collaboration with CPUT-SA Project 3: nanocmposites sysnthesis Tittle • iron-zirconium '
                'nanocomposite for the remediation of emerging pollutants in river nyakomisaro, in kisii county kenya, '
                'Collaboration with UKZN-SA project 4/: green and sustainable chemistry tittle: • Production of '
                'biohydrogen from fermented bioethanol from waste banana peel and pineapple through catalytic '
                'convertor Collaboration CSTI_UJ 6. Publications: Journals • Waketola AG, Hone FG, Mola GT, Oseni SO, '
                'Ogutu H., Tegegne NA, Hybrid silver/silver-oxide nanoparticle doped hole transport layer for the '
                'effective photon harvesting in organic solar cells, Applied Physics A 129 (2), 96, 2023 '
                'https://doi.org/10.1007/s00339-022-06349-4 • Lwazi Ndlwana , Naledi Raleie, Kgogobi M. Dimpe, Hezron '
                'F. Ogutu, Ekemena O. Oseghe, Mxolisi M. Motsa, Titus A.M. Msagati and Bhekie B. Mamba Hydrothermal '
                'and Solvothermal Synthesis of Advanced Carbon Materials in Multidimensional Applications: A Review:. '
                'Materials 2021, 14, 5094. https://doi.org/10.3390/ma14175094 • Brendan H. P, Ogutu Hezron F.O., Saban '
                'Waheed, Luckay Robert C. Synthesis, characterization and use of imidazole and methyl-pyrazole based '
                'pyridine ligands as extractants for nickel(II) and copper(II) Inorganica Chimica Acta 490 (2019) '
                '57–67 https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ica.2019.02.020: • Ogutu HFO, Saban W, Malgas-Enus R, Luckay R.C, '
                'Design, synthesis and spectroscopic characterization of mixed N-and O-donor Schiff base ligands '
                '(N2O3): Crystal structures of free, ligands:: Journal of Molecular Structure 20120, 1211, 1281061: '
                'https://doi.org/10.1016/j.molstruc.2020.128106 • Ogutu Hezron F.O., Saban Waheed, Malgas-Enus '
                'Rehana,. Luckay Robert C Synthesis and characterization of 5- and 7-donor Schiff base and '
                'spectroscopic evidence for tautomerism: A crystal structure showing tautomeric forms within one '
                'ligand Journal of Molecular Structure 1185 (2019) 392e402 '
                'https://doi.org/10.1016/j.molstruc.2019.02.054 • Brendan H. p, Ogutu, Hezron. F. Luckay Robert C: '
