                'and Media, and Kiswahili Subject Methods Close Dr. Evelyn W Njurai Lecturer Read Bio Dr. Evelyn W '
                'Njurai Bio × • Doctor in Mathematics Education • Department of Curriculum, Instruction and Media '
                'Biography: • Evelyn is a lecturer of Curriculum Studies and Mathematics Education courses. She is '
                'currently the coordinator of Teaching Practice and previously served as the Head of Department for '
                'Curriculum, Instruction and Media. She has actively participated in curriculum review both in basic '
                'and higher education in mathematics and mathematics education in Kenya. Evelyn has participated in '
                'various workshops to enhance her knowledge and skills for professional growth.She is a members of '
                'various professional bodies which include Women Education Researchers of Kenya (WERK), Educational '
                'Management Society of Kenya (EMSK), Forum for African Women Educationalist – Kenya (FAWEK), and FOVET '
                'Researchers. Academic Qualifications: • Doctor of Philosophy - Mathematics Education, 2016 , '
                'University of South Africa, South Africa, Title of thesis: Language Practices of Trilingual '
                'Undergraduate Students Engaging with Mathematics in Kenya • Master of Science – Pure Mathematics, '
                '2007 , Kenyatta University, Kenya • Bachelor of Science – Education (Mathematics and Geography) , '
                '1994, Egerton University, Kenya • Kenya Advanced Certificate of Education; 1989 , Kabare Girls High '
                'School, Kenya • Kenya Certificate of education; 1987 , Kiaritha-ini Secondary School, Kenya • '
                'Certificate of Primary Education; 1983 , St Micheals Girls Primary School, Kenya Research Interests: '
                'Evelyn’s research interests include Mathematics education in context of language diversity, use of '
                'technology for mathematics instruction, STEM, curriculum and emerging issues in and for education. '
                'Pre-Service Teachers’ Pedagogical Knowledge and Perceptions of Climate Change Education- funded by '
                'self and co-researcher DrBilliahGisore Publications: Books 1. Competence Based Curriculum: A Handbook '
                'for Teacher Education: (2023) Posterity Publishers, Eldoret, Oranga. &Ngwacho G.A (editors) 2. '
                'Dictionary of Mathematics for Secondary Schools in Kenya (2019). Nairobi: Kenya Literautre Bureau. 3. '
                'Impacts of Globalization and Innovations in Mathematics Education(in press 2024) Copyright © 2024, '
                'IGI Global., Alphonse Uworwabayeho (editors). Book Chapters 1. Responsible Conduct of Research in a '
                'Globalized World: Challenges and Strategies (2024). In Challenges of Globalization and Inclusivity in '
                'Academic Research. Copyright © 2024, IGI Global DOI: 10.4018/979-8-3693-1371-8.ch015, C0-authors; '
                'Billiah Nyamoita Gisore, George Ngwacho Areba, Josephine Oranga, 2. Pre-service teachers’ pedagogical '
