                'Bio × • Dr. GRACE ATEMI ONDIEKI • SEDHURED, EDUCATIONAL PSYCHOLOGY Biography: Dr. Grace Atemi Ondieki '
                'is a lecturer in Educational Psychology at Kisii University and served as the coordinator of '
                'undergraduate studies at the Kericho Campus and School of Education postgraduate studies Main Campus. '
                'Her academic achievements include a PHD in Educational Psychology from Moi University, M. Ed. '
                'Educational Psychology from Kenyatta University, and a B. Ed. English and Literature from Moi '
                'University. She is an active member of the International Society for the study of Behavioural '
                'Development (ISSBD), EMSK and the Kenya Guidance Counselling and Psychological Association. Her '
                'research interests is in childcare. Academic Qualifications: Doctor of philosophy in Educational '
                'Psychology; Moi University, Eldoret. 2014. Master of Education in Educational Psychology - Kenyatta '
                'University. 2006. Bachelor of Education-English and Literature - Moi University. 1994 Theses: Masters '
                '(Factors Influencing Drug Abuse among Youths in Secondary Schools). PhD: Preventive (Measures of Drug '
                'Abuse among Youths in Secondary Schools) Research Interests: • Overview – brief summary of your areas '
                'of research interests and achievements, • Title of Main Research Projects –indicate if they are '
                'funded by whom and /or collaborative with whom, etc. Publications: Atemi, G.O., (2022). '
                'Abakhabillisi. Utafiti Foundation (ISBN: 978-9966-26-260-8) Eldoret. Kenya (Book) Atemi, G.O., '
                '(2018). The Banyore Folktale: Utafiti Foundation (ISBN: 978-9966-26-106-9) Eldoret. Kenya (Book) Book '
                'Chapters Atemi, G.O., (2024). Priscilla Were: Pioneer Educationist and Longest Serving Principal of '
                'Bunyore Girls High School Book Chapter in African Women and Intellectual Leadership Life Stories from '
                'Western Kenya ISBN 9781032279893 280 Pages February 29, 2024 by Routledge '
                'Conferences/Lectures/Workshops 28th May to30th May 2024: Attended a sensitization workshop for staff '
                'on ISO 9001:2015 QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM PERFORMANCE CONTRACTING AND SERVICE DELIVERY held at '
                'senate chambers kisii university 22nd May 2024: attended “How to Publish with Oxford Journal” held '
                'virtually 18th September to 22nd September 2023: Attended eLearning training held at ICT village '
                'conference room and learned: Course Navigation, Content organization, Activity creation, Assessment '
                'strategies, Communication tools, Feedback mechanisms, Assignment submission, Course enrolment, Media '
                'Integration, Assessment security, Attendance tracking, Backup and restore 10th to 12th August 2023. '
                'The 15th ISSBD African Regional Workshop, Uganda at KYAMBOGO University 13th July 2023 Exploring '
                'Dominant Discourses of Work, Education and Gender: Young Women in Rural Nigeria Navigating Education '
                'and Work, held at ICT Village, Kisii University. 5th July 2023 Sensitization workshop on ISO '
                '9001:2015 QUALITY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM, PERFORMANCE MANAGEMENT AND STRATEGIC PLANNING held at DALLAS '
                'PREMIER HOTEL, KISII o August 2023: Worn an international grant (Ksh.100,000) that covered workshop '
