                'Computer Science, 7(5), 1-6. Official Contact Details: • University Email: '
                'dketui@kisiiuniversity.ac.ke Close Dr. Erick Rayora Nyakundi Lecturer Read Bio Dr. Erick Rayora '
                'Nyakundi Bio × • Dr. Erick Rayora Nyakundi • Doctor of Geophysics Biography: Dr. Rayora is a lecturer '
                'and researcher, department of Physics at Kisii University. He carried out research on heat flow, '
                'gravity and magnetic methods to characterize geothermal heat sources. He studied and researched on '
                'geophysical data processing techniques namely; Fast Fourier analysis, Euler deconvolution, Spectral '
                'analysis and forward modelling. His specific study areas include: Physics of the Earth’ s interior, '
                'Applied geophysics, Computer application and geophysical data analysis. He is interested in the study '
                'of geothermal technology using Seismic, Electrical, and Electromagnetic techniques. Furthermore, he '
                'is a member of the Society of Exploration Geophysicists and Geothermal Association of Kenya. Academic '
                'Qualifications: • Ph.D (Physics), 2022, Jomo Kenyatta University of Agriculture and Technology. • Msc '
                '(Physics), 2017, Kenyatta University. • Bed Science, 2010, Moi University. • KCSE, 2004, Kenya '
                "National Examination Council. Research Interests: Dr. Rayora's research interests feature the "
                'utilization of geophysical field methods such as Seismic, Electrical, and Electromagnetic techniques '
                "in advancing geothermal technology. Publications: • Ombati, D., Githiri, J., K'Orowe, M., & Nyakundi, "
                'E. (2022). Delineation of Subsurface Structures Using Gravity Data of the Shallow Offshore, Lamu '
                'Basin, Kenya. Hindawi International Journal of Geophysics. doi: https://doi.org/10.1155/2022/3024977 '
                '• Nyakundi, E. R., Gitonga, G. J., & K’Orowe, M. O. (2021). Simultaneous Modelling of Gravity and '
                'Magnetic Data in a Measured Heat Flux Area to Characterize Geothermal Heat Sources: A Case for Eburru '
                'Geothermal Complex, Kenya. Journal of geoscience and environment protection, 2021(9), 40-54. doi: '
                "10.4236/gep.2021.95005 • Nyakundi, E. R., Githiri, J., & K'Orowe, M. (2020). Depth Estimation of "
                'Geothermal Heat Structures by Euler Deconvolution of Gravity Data at Eburru Area, Kenya. Journal of '
                'geoscience and environment protection, 2020(8), 148-158. doi: 10.4236/gep.2020.83011 • Ombati, D., '
                'Willis, A., John, G., & Nyakundi, E. (2020). Geo-Electrical Resistivity Investigation of Mineral '
                'Bearing Rocks in Rongo Gold Mining Area in Migori County. Journal of Applied Geology and Geophysics '
                "(IOSR-JAGG), 8(4), 28-40. doi: 10.9790/0990-080402284 • Nyakundi, E. R., Githiri, J., K'Orowe, M., & "
                'Ombati, D. (2019). Spectral Analysis of Ground Magnetic Data Using Fast Fourier Transform In Eburru, '
                'Southern Rift, Kenya. Journal of Applied Geology and Geophysics, 7(5), 60-66. doi: '
                '10.9790/0990-0705026066 • Nyakundi, E. R., Githiri, J., & Ambuso, W. (2017). Geophysical '
                'investigation of geothermal potential of the Gilgil area, Nakuru county, Kenya using gravity. journal '
                'of geology and geophysics, 6(2). doi: 10.4172/2381-8719.1000278 Conferences 12th – 17th July, 2022: '
                'Attended The Kenya Geothermal Congress at Emara Ole-Sereni Convention Centre, Nairobi, Kenya. 6th - '
                '7th November, 2018: Attended the 2ND International Forum on Geothermal Technology at Jomo Kenyatta '
                'University of Agriculture and Technology, Nairobi, Kenya. Classes taugth: • PHYS 813: Classical '
                'Mechanics • PHYS 821: Thermodynamics and Statistical Physics • BSMN 425: Imaging Geophysics • BSMN '
                '418: Engineering Geophysics • BSMN 426: Mineral engineering II • BSMN 416: Seismic stratigraphy • '
                'BSMN 324: Seismic data processing and interpretation. • BSMN 315: Potential field theory • BSMN 314: '
                'Applied Geophysics II • BSMN 222: Applied Geophysics I • BSMN 217: Mineralogy and crystallography • '
                'BSMN 121: Geomorphology • BSMN 113: Introduction to Geophysics Other relevant links: '
                'https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=pHn-rR8AAAAJ&hl=en '
                'https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=pHn-rR8AAAAJ&hl=en&oi=ao Official Contact Details: '
                'rayora@kisiiuniversity.ac.ke Close mode_comment close Kisii University Support close Hi Welcome to '
                'Kisii University Customer Care Center. What do you need help with? Raise a ticket Check your ticket '
                'status Raise a complaint Make a compliment Write your suggestion Monitor your feedback status Request '
                'for information Follow up your request Get Service send ABOUT US Vision Mission Our Core values '
                'Service Charter University Council University Managem',
