                'Mrs WINROSE NAFULA WAMALWA-BARASA Assistant lecterer Read Bio Mrs WINROSE NAFULA WAMALWA-BARASA Bio × '
                '• SCHOOL OF BUSINESS AND ECONOMICS • DEPARTMENT OF TOURISM AND HOSPITALITY Biography: PROFESSIONAL '
                'EXPERIENCE Winrose has been a Part-Time lecturer at Cooperative University of Kenya, Africa '
                'International University and Riara University. She is also a Freelance '
                'Translator/editor&proof-reader, K.C.S.E. Examiner Kiswahili Paper 2 and French Paper 3(Oral '
                'examination). Winrose has also been a teacher of French and Kiswahili at Alliance High School. '
                'MEMBERSHIP TO ASSOCIATIONS Winrose is a bonafide member of the Kenya Association of Teachers of '
                'French (KATF) as well as The East Africa Interpreters and Translators Association (EAITA). OTHER '
                'ACHIEVEMENTS Winrose qualified for a scholarship by the African Canadian Continuing Education Society '
                '(ACCES) for post-secondary school education. She also qualified for a scholarship by the Canadian '
                'Harambee Education Society (CHES) for secondary school education as well as a scholarship for Masters '
                'in Translation Studies at the University of Nairobi. She was also nominated by a former student of '
                'Alliance High School for the best teacher and mentor award offered by African Leadership Academy. '
                'Academic Qualifications: 2018-2019: Master of Arts in Translation Studies at the University of '
                'Nairobi Dissertation Topic: The Role of Translation in the Teaching and Learning of French as a '
                'Foreign Language: A Case Study of Selected High Schools in Kenya 2012-2022: Master of Arts in '
                'International Relations and Diplomacy at Kenyatta University Dissertation Topic: Kenya’s Foreign '
                'Policy Towards Ethiopia, 1963-2010 2002-2006 Maseno University B.Ed(Arts) French 2ndClass Honors, '
