                'RESEARCH Website Funding Opportunities External Research Grants Ongoing Research Projects COMPLIMENTS '
                '/ COMPLAINTS CONTACT US Search term Search Kisii University: Web People Search Web Other ways to '
                'search: Map Profiles Dr. Erick Rayora Nyakundi C.O.D, Physics Biography Research Interests My '
                'research interests focus on applied geophysics, geophysical data analysis, and the physics of the '
                "Earth's interior, with particular emphasis on geothermal exploration and technology. I am interested "
                'in the integration of gravity, magnetic, seismic, electrical, and electromagnetic methods for '
                'subsurface imaging and characterization of geothermal systems. My research also explores the '
                'application of advanced quantitative interpretation techniques, including Fast Fourier Analysis, '
                'Euler Deconvolution, Spectral Analysis, and Joint Forward Modeling, to enhance the understanding of '
                'subsurface geological structures and geothermal resources. Education Background Rigoma secondary '
                'school 2001 - 2004 B+ Jomo Kenyatta University of Agriculture and Technology 2018 Jan - 2022 June '
                'Doctor of Pholosophy(PhD) GEOTHERMAL HEAT SOURCES CHARACTERIZATION AND MAPPING USING HEAT FLOW, '
                'GRAVITY, AND MAGNETICS IN EBURRU, KENYA Kenyatta University 2013 April - 2017 July Masters '
                'GEOPHYSICAL INVESTIGATION OF GEOTHERMAL POTENTIAL OF THE GILGIL AREA, NAKURU COUNTY, KENYA USING '
                'GRAVITY METHOD Moi University 2006 Sep - 2010 Dec Bachelors Work Experience Kisii University July '
                '2017 - Kisii University June 2026 - Kisii University Jan 2024 - Kisii University Feb 2024 - 2024 '
